han Gygax D&amp;D. It is not anything like mage. It does not feel the same, play the same, or have the same tone. If you try to adapt pieces of it to mage, you will wind up giving up mage and playing Ars Magica instead.It does everything you wish mage would do.<br /> <br /> Obviously I have a bias <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/c/play-by-post-campaigns/ars-magica-5th-edition-light-of-andorra/32\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/uploads/default/original/1X/ceadc4b228e55aec49e787add129dcbe5f6a8c70.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/c/play-by-post-campaigns/ars-magica-5th-edition-light-of-andorra/32\" target=\"_blank\"> Ars Magica 5th Edition: Light of Andorra </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/c/play-by-post-campaigns/ars-magica-5th-edition-light-of-andorra/32\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forum.atlas-games.com/c/play-by-post-campaigns/ars-magica-5th-edition-light-of-andorra/32 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Adventure! Glory! Legend and Mystery! This is the bread and butter of the magi of Andorra. But power and prosperity are but mere distractions, and the covenant has some difficult choices and challenges ahead. </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. I\u2019m not very crunchy at all, but I love the setting stuff. One of my old D&amp;D DMs recommended it to me (he loved the formulas lol) and I really like the Tribunal books.<br /> <br /> What happened with House Flambeau?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T12:24:55-07:00","id":1409408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1407266-how-are-ars-magica-and-mage-the-ascension-related?p=1409318#post1409318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been playing Ars Magica for decades and I have even written for the game. I was excited to say a whole bunch of stuff, but others beat me too it, and they are mostly accurate.<br /> <br /> Ars Magica was created by Jonathan Tweet, the same guy who engineered D&amp;D 3rd edition, and it is indeed the very first of its kind as far as a troupe style story focused game with flexible improvised magic along with magic formula. Mark Rein*Hagen joined in with the second edition of that game, published by Lion Rampart, and it begat a strong cult following. Jon Nephew was a major player at Lion Rampart, and wrote some for that edition (as well as a few becmi D&amp;D books). Tweet and Rein*Hagen started sowing the seed for the 0WoD. References to Tremere magi (and some Boniagus) experimenting with the undead can be found in 2nd ed books such as Order of Hermes, Covenants, and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mark Rein-Hagen is credited as a co-creator of the 1st edition, with Jonathan Tweet, and this was also published by Lion Rampart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T13:59:41-07:00","id":1409414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1407266-how-are-ars-magica-and-mage-the-ascension-related?p=1409408#post1409408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mark Rein-Hagen is credited as a co-creator of the 1st edition, with Jonathan Tweet, and this was also published by Lion Rampart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never seen 1st. But I have seen pics of the cover, and you are most correct. 2nd edition is the same. Let me check the others...<br /> They all say Tween &amp; Rein*Hagen. Except Third, which includes a bunch of extra authors that are demoted to &quot;contributor&quot; in 4th. I am a geek, and I own every edition except the rare and elusive 1st. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Most of the &quot;evils&quot; of third edition were actually the work of Ken Cliffe. He was the type of editor who would add parenthetical notes scattered everywhere to sow infernal story seeds (and to imply what was just written may mean the opposite). And so, though it is Rein*Hagen that sliced it up for Vampire, he is not the one who altered the game.In fact, Rein*Hagen had recently showed up in the Ars FB group to ask how we have been handling Auras all these years. It was wrong of me to not assign him co-credit. I mistakenly remembered him as an assistant. Tweet's name sticks in my head because he is the one that created and wrote the Order of Hermes and Houses of Hermes.<br /> <br /> un Fact! Wizards of the Coast had bout Ars Magica and published three &quot;proto-fourth edition&quot; books, one of which is Houses of Hermes. TotC then decided the did not want to be in the RPG business, sold Ars to Atlas, then bought up AD&amp;D and D&amp;D, then in turn they themselves got bought up by Hasbro.<br /> <br /> I know I probably have one or more fact wrong, so please correct me if you have better information <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T14:35:27-07:00","id":1409418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1407266-how-are-ars-magica-and-mage-the-ascension-related?p=1409320#post1409320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome! Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. I\u2019m not very crunchy at all, but I love the setting stuff. One of my old D&amp;D DMs recommended it to me (he loved the formulas lol) and I really like the Tribunal books.<br /> <br /> What happened with House Flambeau?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ars Magica can kinda be seen as the missing link between AD&amp;D and the oWoD. The original Ars Magica had not much of a setting. It was a home brew magic system ment to be tacked on to AD&amp;D. This was back in 1988 or 89. I think. Second, the OTE, is where Mythic Europe and the Order of Hermes are developed. Third created this huge political landscape, because that is what WW games were all about back then. 4th was the retcon and refined the crunchy gurps like quality the game used to have. Fift refined everything and is not gurps like at all any more.<br /> <br /> If you want to hunt around on e-bay, you can find lots of third edition material at a reasonable price. I *love* the art that WW used to put out back then! That is the stuff that is the most related to Mage and the WoD. The mechanics do not translate, but some concepts may. Third edition introduced Twilight, somewhat similar to Paradox in mage. That stuck around in 4th, and in 5th it was revised into a mechanic called Warping. Third is the one with all the story seed connections to Mage also. That is where Mistridge comes from. I have an extra if you want it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Davud Chart, the helmsman for 5th edition, he never wrote for Mage but he is a fan. He was promoting the Tecnocracy kickstarter and mentioned that, though he never wrote for mage, he was proud that his story about the White Tower (in 3rd) still persists as the backstory of that game.<br /> <br /> As for House Flambeau it is a long bitter story.<br /> See, though I started with that game in 4th edition, I also started with a bunch of 3rd ed sourcebooks from the WW era. My favorite is still Tribunals of Hermes-Iberia, by Peter Hentges. That is where the original story of Flambeau comes from. It sparked within me a love of Spanish history and language. 4th ed didn't touch anything there. The main retcon focus there was to reform and reinstate House Tremere and sweep the whole vampire thing under the rug. But they were still fascists. 5th edition did a deep retcon, and House Tremere is actually very interesting and fun to play. And history was respected. Changes were made, but it was recognizable.<br /> <br /> House Flambeau was not treated as gently.<br /> I fought with the guy about it. I blew up the Berklist with flame wars. But I made peace with the guy and wrote a fanzine re-retcon with his help. So, I have no animosity remaining. I am an active member of the fan community, and I have worked hard to insure the original is not forgotten. I demonstrated that ideas can merge. It is okay to retcon, but you should at least honor the original somehow in the new work.<br /> <br /> 3rd edition Flambeau (the founder) was Danny Trejo if he played a part in Magnificent Seven. 5th edition Flambeau (the founder) is Kevin Costner in any bad Kostner movie. His Hispanic identity was removed, and he was white washed into a Frankish dandy..<br /> <br /> Old edition books are PDF only and can be found on Drive through RPG. Hardcopy can be found as resale used books. The current 5th edition is still in print and available from the Atlas Gamessite, as pdf or hardcopy.The three 5th ed books I worked on are Grogs, Tales of Power, and Faith &amp; Flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T14:52:44-07:00","id":1409422,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25651_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25651\" data-vbnamecard=\"25651\">Marko Markoko</a> Awesome! I\u2019m impressed that you used to write for Ars Magica. It\u2019s a really cool game.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been buying up the old Tribunal books in PDF form on Warehouse23, so I\u2019m pretty happy rn. But thank you for the offer \ud83d\ude0a. That\u2019s really nice of you.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sorry about Flambeau. I really liked his origin story in the Iberia Tribunal book. If I ever do anything with him as a character I\u2019ll leave him as Hispanic and maybe make the Frankish dandy version his apprentice Apromor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T16:57:25-07:00","id":1409434,"title":"","content":"Apromor is a Basque, a master of destructive magic and the mastermind that incorporated the Cult of Mercury into the magic of Flambeau <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I already fixed it as well as it can be fixed. In Faith &amp; Flame I introduced a hook about a conspiracy theory and trying to falsify or obscure the truth. It is a conflict between two cults within that House, The Cult of Mercury and the Cult of Mithras. It is a political power struggle over leadership and control of direction.<br /> <br /> I hope that guy doesn't read this forum. I made peace with him. But at the time, some thirteen years ago, I saw it as a continuation of the hysterial fevor to remove and sever any ties with White Wolf. I also wrongly suspected racism, as Flambeau was the only minority Founder (if Iberian counts as Hispanic).<br /> <br /> The anti-White Wolf hysteria continues to this very day, though it is subdued. Some grognards are still bitter over a divorce that happened thirty years ago. There are even those who want to eliminate the Tremere and change the name of the Order of Hermes, just to further distance the game from WW and sever any legal ties. These are the same people that did not know that White Wold was bought out years ago. Every Ars book still prints a TM for White Wolf in reference to the terms Tremere, Order of Hermes, and Doisettep. Though we renamed and restyled Doisettep and there is no need for that any more. Early edition Mage books used to do the same in reverse, for names such as Flambeau, Bonisagus, etc.<br /> <br /> I have asked many people. No one seems to know who owns the TMs to any of these names or terms. I asked Satyros on Facebook, and he said it is a mystery quagmire that is best left untouched. David Chart and Atlas Games don't want to answer the question, lest they say something inaccurate. I don't know if CCP or Onyx path know or care. If anyone *does* know, please enlighten me!<br /> <br /> Though Ars Magica 5 is still in print, the line has ended as of three years ago or so. David Chat wrote that he has taken the game as far as it can go without another new edition, and he has moved on. There are no plans for any new books. Atlas may move forward to a sixth some day. But the line as-is is stable and selling, and for a small niche game company, Atlas has done well for itself. They publish a few other RPGs, such as Feng-Sui and Over the Edge. Most of what they do is card and board games. i reccomend Lost in R'lyeh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T17:46:31-07:00","id":1409439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1407266-how-are-ars-magica-and-mage-the-ascension-related?p=1409434#post1409434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apromor is a Basque, a master of destructive magic and the mastermind that incorporated the Cult of Mercury into the magic of Flambeau <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I already fixed it as well as it can be fixed. In Faith &amp; Flame I introduced a hook about a conspiracy theory and trying to falsify or obscure the truth. It is a conflict between two cults within that House, The Cult of Mercury and the Cult of Mithras. It is a political power struggle over leadership and control of direction.<br /> <br /> I hope that guy doesn't read this forum. I made peace with him. But at the time, some thirteen years ago, I saw it as a continuation of the hysterial fevor to remove and sever any ties with White Wolf. I also wrongly suspected racism, as Flambeau was the only minority Founder (if Iberian counts as Hispanic).<br /> <br /> The anti-White Wolf hysteria continues to this very day, though it is subdued. Some grognards are still bitter over a divorce that happened thirty years ago. There are even those who want to eliminate the Tremere and change the name of the Order of Hermes, just to further distance the game from WW and sever any legal ties. These are the same people that did not know that White Wold was bought out years ago. Every Ars book still prints a TM for White Wolf in reference to the terms Tremere, Order of Hermes, and Doisettep. Though we renamed and restyled Doisettep and there is no need for that any more. Early edition Mage books used to do the same in reverse, for names such as Flambeau, Bonisagus, etc.<br /> <br /> I have asked many people. No one seems to know who owns the TMs to any of these names or terms. I asked Satyros on Facebook, and he said it is a mystery quagmire that is best left untouched. David Chart and Atlas Games don't want to answer the question, lest they say something inaccurate. I don't know if CCP or Onyx path know or care. If anyone *does* know, please enlighten me!<br /> <br /> Though Ars Magica 5 is still in print, the line has ended as of three years ago or so. David Chat wrote that he has taken the game as far as it can go without another new edition, and he has moved on. There are no plans for any new books. Atlas may move forward to a sixth some day. But the line as-is is stable and selling, and for a small niche game company, Atlas has done well for itself. They publish a few other RPGs, such as Feng-Sui and Over the Edge. Most of what they do is card and board games. i reccomend Lost in R'lyeh!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for telling me. I\u2019m still reading the Tribunal books. Which one has the retcon of Flambeau as a Frankish dandy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T23:01:03-07:00","id":1409471,"title":"","content":"Houses of Hermes: Societates for fifth edition. And I exaggerate when i say dandy. I am a horrible critic. It is a good piece of writing. I like how the systems and practices were enhanced. It is a good book. I am a terrible person that is holding a gaming grudge thirteen years old. Do not pay that much attention to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T23:23:20-07:00","id":1409475,"title":"","content":"For me, the best Ars Magica books that would translate well into Mage: The Ascension - because they help focus on paradigm building rather than rules - are The Mysteries and Art &amp; Academe. The former is the straight beef on the Hermetic paradigm, and the latter also builds on it through detailing with medieval philosophy and practices. Each are very well researched (to Ph.D level, really) and based on real world studies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:23:36-07:00","id":1409522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1407266-how-are-ars-magica-and-mage-the-ascension-related?p=1409471#post1409471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Houses of Hermes: Societates for fifth edition. And I exaggerate when i say dandy. I am a horrible critic. It is a good piece of writing. I like how the systems and practices were enhanced. It is a good book. I am a terrible person that is holding a gaming grudge thirteen years old. Do not pay that much attention to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T08:21:43-07:00","id":1409564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1407266-how-are-ars-magica-and-mage-the-ascension-related?p=1409418#post1409418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I blew up the Berklist with flame wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only possible response one would expect from House Flambeau.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}